<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore February M1 rises 6.9 pct on year - MAS.</title>
<headline>Singapore February M1 rises 6.9 pct on year - MAS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Money supply figures.</p>
<p>	   (in billions of Singapore dollars)</p>
<p>				  Feb	Jan    Feb '96</p>
<p>M-1 (narrow money)	 27.92    28.85   26.12</p>
<p>M-2			   113.66   113.06  102.73</p>
<p>M-3 (broad money)	 141.87   141.70  129.15</p>
<p>Demand deposits	    17.06   17.84     15.85</p>
<p>Currency in active	 10.86   11.01     10.27</p>
<p>circulation</p>
<p>Note - The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said narrow money supply (M1) grew by 6.9 percent year-on-year in February, compared with 9.9 percent in January.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
